{"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the layer model and rendering pipeline of TUIkit.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/RenderCycle"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit is structured in six layers, each building on the one below. This clean separation makes the framework easy to extend and maintain."}]},{"text":"Layer Model","type":"heading","anchor":"Layer-Model","level":2},{"text":"1. App Layer","type":"heading","anchor":"1-App-Layer","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/App","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol is the entry point. It defines one or more scenes that make up your application. The internal "},{"code":"AppRunner","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" manages the async event loop, terminal setup, signal handling, and event dispatching."}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["@main → App → AppRunner → RuntimeEventChannel"]},{"text":"2. View Layer","type":"heading","anchor":"2-View-Layer","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every UI component conforms to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/View","type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol. Views are composed declaratively using ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ViewBuilder","type":"reference"},{"text":", which supports:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single and multiple child views (up to 10)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlin